@flexiarg war-room/wr-24-a-removed-constraint-does-not-remove-the-discipline-it-supplied
@title WR-24: A Removed Constraint Does Not Remove the Discipline It Supplied
@sigils [⚖/令]
@audience futon stack operators, agents, mission authors
@tone foundational
@style pattern
@references [war-room/wr-27-a-loop-is-born-instrumented-for-its-gain]

! conclusion: When retiring a proxy constraint, install its replacement discipline in the same act and measure how much external verdict content changes subsequent work, not merely whether a verdict arrived.

  + context: War Room decision WR-24 (2026-07-30). Operator: Joe. The same-day gain revision is carried forward and later generalized by WR-27.

  + IF:
    A gate was installed as a proxy for another requirement, such as using a cash gate as the cheapest available proxy for external validity, and the underlying scarcity is lifted.

  + HOWEVER:
    Silently removing the pressure also removes its arbitration discipline. Pleasant, active pi-hermit behavior can then look like progress from inside even when outward feedback does not affect what gets built.

  + THEN:
    Name the replacement in the same act as retirement. Replace the cash gate's master role with witnessed external verdict, using compiler, maintainer, peer-review, and money instruments; measure the gate as the graded gain from verdict content into the next decision, not as a weekly yes-or-no event.

  + BECAUSE:
    External evaluation cannot be self-supplied, but a boolean gate on an impoverished predicate buys nothing over simply continuing the work. The governing quantity is how much returned content changes the genotype or plan.

    + evidence: War Bulletin 14 Finding 4 identifies the lost disciplinary function and three working external-verdict instruments. Its same-day addendum reports that TN-coupling-gain found reach graded by phenotype-to-genotype gain while eight other coordinates were silent, and that the mobility-matched blind control remained ordered despite equal outward movement.
